{"event_type":"review","id":"fb32a5b94665504fb68790c4cb4c4a9b566ddd498394f0285f665c47b4472c4f","occurred_at":"2026-11-17T22:28:31Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/6efae3e9e2ec2373dfbc878543f58f4b17600a84a8d7eba5f6effddb2dea1c91","sha256":"6efae3e9e2ec2373dfbc878543f58f4b17600a84a8d7eba5f6effddb2dea1c91"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/a4144f64ce4ae6b875b42c61090beee5647e96ac5f77ac76ccea0c711b814110","sha256":"a4144f64ce4ae6b875b42c61090beee5647e96ac5f77ac76ccea0c711b814110"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/f3fb6aaf0265e5dc10b811a069afee2533b1256ebf5bf4a382b4cae163442b7b","sha256":"f3fb6aaf0265e5dc10b811a069afee2533b1256ebf5bf4a382b4cae163442b7b"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/f07e84359c5a59f42875e6da70c8c8db90262734b6fd09b65d191534f8c95b84","sha256":"f07e84359c5a59f42875e6da70c8c8db90262734b6fd09b65d191534f8c95b84"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/24694476d90d23dad82c7d16c31c98bc1591835cae2bc2efb92e8eeabb9e1f13","sha256":"24694476d90d23dad82c7d16c31c98bc1591835cae2bc2efb92e8eeabb9e1f13"}],"attempt_id":"e3e34c0989780a4fde0595190d494ae5fd5bfef1daaf8c456a70423d58b1101d:0:1","base":"b45afb5575084d78ede083d19719fd9d899c84a3","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"4f5ba60d61b9f198f16cfed7a39e3aac06df4fed","body":"**These refusal tests never prove that no managed dispatch happened.**\n\nNeither test passes a counting `managedSubmit`. `reviewerCalls` counts only `coderabbit` command spawns, which the managed route does not make. The scan-policy test at Line 127 asserts only `needs-human` and \"no reuse record\". It does not assert the absence of a fresh dispatch. A regression could fall through to a fresh managed cycle, and the test would still pass if that cycle also returned `needs-human`.\n\nThe retained-log learning requires that content the current scanner forbids \"refuses review without dispatch\". The ledger-fault test at Line 356 has the same gap. Other tests in this file already use a `managedCalls` counter or a throwing submit (Line 383).\n\nPass `vi.fn(managedTerminal())` as the fourth `cycleReview` argument in both tests. Assert `toHaveBeenCalledTimes(0)`. For Line 127, also assert that the reason names `new-policy-rule`.\n\nAs per path instructions, `test/**`: \"Prefer assertions that exercise intended behavior and its failure modes … over shape-only checks.\"\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAlso applies to: 369-369","id":"917cd2e662f0453c0d70c99dbd2217b96b19ddd2f8389d356d55d8851044b90f","intervals":[[137,137]],"path":"test/ops/dev/reviewCycleProvenanceReuse.test.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"These refusal tests never prove that no managed dispatch happened."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"6bad1bc2bb35e7b453eba50852310228f8d19152","body":"**`reviewerCalls` cannot detect a managed dispatch, so the \"scan gates the submit\" claims are unverified.**\n\n`reviewerCalls` in `test/ops/dev/reviewTestKit.ts:158-159` filters `effects.calls` for the command `coderabbit`. These tests pass `managedTerminal()`, an in-process scripted function that never goes through `effects.runCommand`. The learning on `docs/coderabbit-review.md` says the SDK no longer launches the CLI directly. If `makeReviewCycle` calls the managed submit before the scan gate, or ignores the gate, these assertions still pass.\n\nLine 149 (scanner hit) has no ledger assertion either. It relies only on the refusal reason. The test titled \"THE SCAN GATES THE SUBMIT\" never proves that the submit was not called.\n\nWrap the submit in `vi.fn(managedTerminal())` and assert `expect(submit).not.toHaveBeenCalled()`. Line 93 already uses this pattern. Keep `reviewerCalls` only if you also want to assert that no CLI launch occurs.\n\nAs per path instructions, `test/**`: \"Prefer assertions that exercise intended behavior and its failure modes … over shape-only checks.\"\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAlso applies to: 149-149, 162-162, 179-179","id":"0b3b391a3509c994c935c4e72144ccb5dd0f29ac5b34ac296aa85fbb638b248f","intervals":[[81,81]],"path":"test/ops/dev/reviewCycleScanExclusions.test.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"`reviewerCalls` cannot detect a managed dispatch, so the \"scan gates the submit\" claims are unverified."}],"head":"97cbeecdd0961e80c3c0372e27b6d92ccf55a563","head_tree":"12e1095fbecea104e28eb07c86b1760f1f72bd77","input_scope":[{"blob":"7bdce60a72fcd094720844408a80fd056e4014dd","intervals":[[1,519]],"path":"test/ops/dev/cycle-usage.test.ts"},{"blob":"bd800a2ed9c5481cc57a7bed5fda442d4a17f0a7","intervals":[[1,611]],"path":"test/ops/dev/denylist.test.ts"},{"blob":"d1476dbc6397107cc67ad7cd8cc4803861690c4a","intervals":[[1,657]],"path":"test/ops/dev/managedReview.test.ts"},{"blob":"c1b30356439175484ef95c08b57ee8123cd24859","intervals":[[1,230]],"path":"test/ops/dev/registry.test.ts"},{"blob":"3bbe99df060f8e5ab30af64a55ab3e2fd782ba23","intervals":[[1,260]],"path":"test/ops/dev/reviewBudgetAttribution.test.ts"},{"blob":"1c2d3ef7346dc7dbe8a193eb3352a0f2b4116b5c","intervals":[[1,420]],"path":"test/ops/dev/reviewCycleAgentEngine.test.ts"},{"blob":"4f5ba60d61b9f198f16cfed7a39e3aac06df4fed","intervals":[[1,437]],"path":"test/ops/dev/reviewCycleProvenanceReuse.test.ts"},{"blob":"6bad1bc2bb35e7b453eba50852310228f8d19152","intervals":[[1,194]],"path":"test/ops/dev/reviewCycleScanExclusions.test.ts"}],"job_id":"e3e34c0989780a4fde0595190d494ae5fd5bfef1daaf8c456a70423d58b1101d:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"7bdce60a72fcd094720844408a80fd056e4014dd","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"test/ops/dev/cycle-usage.test.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"metho